Subject: [PATCH 01/27] prime: sketch a signed template-authorship claim and a
 sovereignty bonus (rnd/a2)

R&D only (P-003 A2, XBT-051); nothing in primed calls either module.

datum-wire::authorship: a gateway adds a zero-value OP_RETURN
"XTA\x01" | ed25519 pk | sig over (domain, height, prev hash, template
root, outputs digest). The template root is the merkle root with a zero
coinbase txid, so Prime gets it from the job's branches and anyone gets
it from the block's txids. The claim still classifies as a Split, and
Prime can require the session's identity key.

tides::sovereignty: bonus pot from the stratum fee (clamped under
fee - rebate) plus an optional differential on unsigned DATUM work,
shared pro rata by authored work as carry; no deferral, Sybil-neutral.

